Terraform Configuration Files
Terraform automatically reads all .tf files in a directory. Structuring these files properly helps teams manage infrastructure efficiently.

Common Terraform Files:
main.tf → Defines the core infrastructure logic
provider.tf → Specifies the cloud provider (AWS, Azure, GCP, etc.)
variables.tf → Stores input values for flexibility and reusability
outputs.tf → Captures output values to use in other modules or for reporting
Tip: File names don’t matter to Terraform; what matters is the content.

✔️Enables Infrastructure as Code (IaC), reducing manual errors and deployment time
✔️Improves scalability and repeatability across environments
✔️Supports collaboration in DevOps teams with modular and reusable code

✔️Deploying multi-tier cloud environments automatically (e.g., VPCs, subnets, EC2 instances)
✔️Integrating with CI/CD pipelines for automated deployments
✔️Managing cloud resources in production, staging, and dev environments with minimal effort
